            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "/**\n * ============================================================================\n * @file curvature-shaper.gendsp / curvature-shaper.maxpat\n * @title CURVATURE-SHAPER (Symmetric S-Curve & Exact Inverse Interpolator)\n * @author Max Bruckert\n *\n * @description\n * Interpolates between two values (a, b) using a symmetric dual-curve function\n * controlled by a bipolar 'shape' parameter:\n *   - shape > 0 : S-curve (exponential ease-in on entry [0..0.5], exact\n *                 mirror inverse ease-out on exit [0.5..1])\n *   - shape = 0 : Pure linear interpolation\n *   - shape < 0 : Exact functional inverse S-curve (logarithmic ease-out on\n *                 entry toward 0.5 plateau, exponential ease-in on exit)\n *\n * Mathematical property: f(-shape, f(+shape, x)) == x for all x in [0, 1].\n *\n * @inlets\n *   in1 : Normalized interpolation phase / ramp (0.0 to 1.0)\n *   in2 : Optional signal-rate additive modulation to 'shape'\n *\n * @outlets\n *   out1 : Interpolated value between a and b\n *   out2 : Normalized shaped curve (0.0 to 1.0)\n *\n * @parameters\n *   a         (default: 0)        : Start value at x = 0\n *   b         (default: 1)        : End value at x = 1\n *   shape     (-1..1, def: 0)     : Bipolar curvature (+: S-curve, -: inverse)\n *   steepness (0.5..10, def: 4)   : Max exponent scaling (2^(shape * steepness))\n *   clamp_in  (0..1, def: 1)      : Clamp input phase strictly to [0, 1]\n * ============================================================================\n */\n\nParam a(0);\nParam b(1);\nParam shape(0, min=-1, max=1);\nParam steepness(4.0, min=0.5, max=10.0);\nParam clamp_in(1, min=0, max=1);\n\nx = (clamp_in >= 0.5) ? clamp(in1, 0.0, 1.0) : in1;\ns_eff = clamp(shape + in2, -1.0, 1.0);\n\n// Symmetric power exponent: p = 1 at shape=0, p > 1 for S-curve, 1/p for inverse\np = pow(2.0, s_eff * steepness);\n\ncurved = 0.0;\nif (x <= 0.0) {\n    curved = 0.0;\n} else if (x >= 1.0) {\n    curved = 1.0;\n} else if (x < 0.5) {\n    // Entry half [0 .. 0.5]: exponential ease-in (p > 1) or log ease-out (p < 1)\n    curved = 0.5 * pow(2.0 * x, p);\n} else {\n    // Exit half [0.5 .. 1]: exact point-symmetric mirror inverse\n    curved = 1.0 - 0.5 * pow(2.0 * (1.0 - x), p);\n}\n\nout1 = mix(a, b, curved);\nout2 = curved;",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
